# SUPPLYLENS
### Understand every dependency in your project.

SupplyLens is a local-first software dependency intelligence tool that helps developers understand the third-party packages used inside their projects.

It analyzes npm package manifests and lockfiles, builds direct and transitive dependency relationships, visualizes dependency trees, detects duplicated package versions, identifies dependency inconsistencies, and generates machine-readable software component inventories.

IMPORTANT:

This must be a real working developer tool, not a dashboard mockup.

The application must parse actual uploaded project files and calculate all statistics using parsed dependency data.

Do not use hardcoded scan results.

Do not pretend to detect vulnerabilities without a genuine vulnerability database.

Do not make external requests to package registries or upload project files.

All analysis must happen locally in the browser.

