==================================================
8. NPM LOCKFILE PARSER
==================================================

This is the MOST IMPORTANT ENGINEERING COMPONENT.

Implement genuine parsers for:

A. package-lock.json version 3.
B. package-lock.json version 2.
C. package-lock.json version 1 where practical.
D. npm-shrinkwrap.json using compatible lockfile structures.

For lockfile versions 2 and 3:

Parse the packages object.

Each entry can contain:

- Package location.
- Package name.
- Package version.
- Dependencies.
- Dev dependencies.
- Optional dependencies.
- Peer dependencies.
- Resolved metadata.
- Integrity metadata.
- License metadata if present.
- Development/optional flags.
- Link/workspace metadata.

Do not assume every package has every field.

Handle scoped package names correctly.

Examples:

@types/node
@tanstack/react-query
react
typescript

For lockfile v1:

Parse the nested dependencies object recursively.

Preserve nested package relationships and resolved versions where available.

IMPORTANT:

Do not simply count dependency names from package.json and pretend this is the installed dependency tree.

The lockfile is the primary source for resolved package versions.

When no supported lockfile exists:

- Parse package.json.
- Show declared direct dependencies.
- Show declared version ranges.
- Set analysis mode to MANIFEST ONLY.
- Do not fabricate resolved versions.
- Do not fabricate transitive dependencies.
- Clearly explain that the resolved dependency tree is unavailable.

